{"id": "EUVD-2026-76460", "enisaUuid": "ea01a80f-0e67-31b2-92eb-ba157d3518fd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsunrpc: route to a populated pool in svc_pool_for_cpu()\n\nsvc_set_num_threads() spreads the requested threads evenly across the\nservice's pools (base = nrservs / sv_nrpools).  When a service runs\nfewer threads than it has pools -- e.g. an nfsd configured with fewer\nthreads than the host has NUMA nodes while running in \"pernode\" or\n\"percpu\" mode -- the trailing pools are left with no threads at all.\n\nsvc_xprt_enqueue() selects a pool from the CPU servicing the transport,\nqueues the transport on that pool's sp_xprts, and only wakes a thread\nfrom the same pool.  Each thread services exclusively its own pool, so a\ntransport that lands on a threadless pool is enqueued on sp_xprts and\nnever picked up: the connection hangs indefinitely.\n\nHave svc_pool_for_cpu() skip pools that currently have no threads,\nfalling back to the next populated pool.  This trades NUMA locality for\na guarantee that the work is actually serviced.  sp_nrthreads is only\nupdated under the service mutex; the lockless read here is a best-effort\nrouting hint, so annotate it with data_race().", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:42", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9accc25e5af0bac8479f6054e674b2c593c45281", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f66d38e2a6c78d48723ea17ad86135ec80ca24b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d79d7b9e8acbb53e2d60f6b24afc13e2f15e691f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edb20e8c03aebacb409968c99d046f509c6c485a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/011479cf9a7657d4a3e7cc42a784ac63df594170", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d04d64ad192439835ed9884d767353061c3ed6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f766d2d0b4dabf54f8b35812df2b4f481d13316", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6310491c4cdb88af73aa551ec9df1f10a90c709"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89549", "GHSA-j6w6-qx29-46gg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cec898a-d842-3844-9679-5b842778f4d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "1f24cb09-247c-3fa2-bf72-4f480b30b37a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bfd241600a3b0db4fe43c859f1460d0a958d924a <8f766d2d0b4dabf54f8b35812df2b4f481d13316"}, {"id": "25a8c766-2fa5-3743-ae81-3d574b38bbdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bfd241600a3b0db4fe43c859f1460d0a958d924a <edb20e8c03aebacb409968c99d046f509c6c485a"}, {"id": "4f2cbcdc-ad41-305d-a2be-f5c0a3cea2a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bfd241600a3b0db4fe43c859f1460d0a958d924a <9d04d64ad192439835ed9884d767353061c3ed6f"}, {"id": "5e2801ad-d124-3121-9fa3-3ae827ad02b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "63c75b7e-ea7c-3a4b-ba29-d8efb6d9ac03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "693eef1a-7978-344a-a9cf-00a55fd85a95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "9a6ef549-0d13-30dd-aac8-90e928e059ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.19"}, {"id": "9b618d70-43c5-3081-8b4e-6426524c72da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9bbfa808-ba33-360b-add5-955cdae5b063", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "beb9993e-6477-3bf5-9ece-411b8fc1adf2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "c7901e3c-7e45-33a9-843f-7866db5298a6", "p